# Project boundaries

This rule is subordinate, in order, to `AGENTS.md`, current explicit owner
decisions, and current roadmap/task authority. Use the current checkout root;
do not assume a machine-specific absolute path.

The Dramatica-Informed Writing Assistant is local-first and analysis-only. It
may store, edit, save, reload, and organize owner-authored prose and project
materials, but AI must never write, rewrite, continue, imitate, polish,
improve, expand, outline, draft, revise, or otherwise generate story prose.

Use the standard refusal message exactly when applicable:

```text
I can analyze structure and ask diagnostic questions, but I cannot write or rewrite story prose.
```

Owner-authored saves must not be overblocked. Analysis output, candidates,
schema validity, confidence, review state, and promotion records do not
establish project truth. Never promote or apply promotion automatically.

The apply-promotion workflow is implemented as a separate explicit and audited
path. It may write approved project-local Memory/Canon only after owner
approval, destination choice, blocker validation, and final confirmation.
Analysis, candidate creation, review status, and promotion creation remain
non-mutating.

The app-owned `dramatica_flow_informed_rubric` is the approved MVP boundary for
permitted analysis-only dramatica-flow-derived concepts and reasoning. It must
never be treated as proof that the external runtime ran. External
`dramatica_flow` is not MVP-required and needs separate explicit owner
authorization plus an analysis-only safety review for any future integration.

Official paid Subtxt/Dramatica is optional. Other integration status and real
execution requirements come from the current roadmap/task authority, not this
client rule.

Fine-tuning, datasets, live models, extractors, external services, and runtime
mutation may be used only when the active task explicitly authorizes them.
